    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's good that your chest pressure isn't acute, but taking these measures voluntarily could delay proper diagnosis and treatment if needed. For minor travel fatigue symptoms, eating well, drinking water, light stretching, and taking acetaminophen, like Tylenol, should help. If you don't have a rise in temperature or your symptoms persist, schedule an appointment with a family physician or a urologist. If symptoms persist, seek medical attention. You can call ahead and ask about making an after-hours appointment online on the the Orthopaedic Association of North America website. You can also visit urgent care if that's more urgent since the emergency room is designed for more severe problems. I know you're feeling exhausted, but it's better to be safe than sorry. I hope you're feeling better soon, I got your back.",
